<code>assert this.get(0).equals(item);</code>

However, based on the natural language assertion, it seems like there might be a misunderstanding. The comment states "the added element is stored at the first position," which would imply the element is at index 0. But in a stack, the top of the stack is the last element added, not the first. Therefore, the correct interpretation should be that the added element is at the last position, which is the top of the stack.

Given this, the correct assert statement should be:

<code>assert this.get(this.size() - 1).equals(item);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.peek().equals(item);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.peek().equals(item);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.peek().equals(item);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.peek().equals(item);</code>
